  "step_1": "The decision reason involves adjusting the probabilities of outcomes with less than 20% probability by increasing their weight by 10 percentage points (i.e., adding 0.10 to their objective probability), then computing a weighted sum of outcomes using these adjusted probabilities. This adjusted expected value determines the preferred lottery. In this decision problem: \n- Lottery A has two outcomes: 1000 Euros (50% probability), 0 Euros (50% probability). Neither outcome has a probability below 20%, so no adjustment is applied. The weighted sum is 1000 × 0.5 + 0 × 0.5 = 500 Euros.\n- Lottery B has one outcome: 500 Euros (100% probability). The probability is 100%, which is above 20%, so no adjustment is applied. The weighted sum is 500 × 1 = 500 Euros.\nThus, both lotteries have the same adjusted expected value (500 Euros), so the reason would be indifferent between them. However, the reason could still be applied, as the relevant probabilities and outcomes are available and the rule is executable.",
